# S3a: the first packed-4 rounds judged for exactness on the four-card S2 engine: the gate's matrix plan on c2-packed-tp4-gate,
# four real-text users (4,096 / 16,384 / 32,768 / 60,000 tokens, 512 tokens out), a concurrent arm (all four at once: packed-4
# rounds) and a solo arm (the same prompts one at a time), under the strict policy: every concurrent text must equal its solo
# text. Every audit the profile carries is on (the T1 shard argmax against the pinned sampler, T2, the proposal audit, the extent
# audit), so this is exactness against the four-card pinned computations, and concurrent == solo is the same-image baseline a new
# width gets. Each arm's acceptance report logs the tokens committed per round (the [ACCEPT] line, mean and per user): the 200
# tok/s plan's W-1 baseline on real text at the bfloat8 drafter.
# There is no four-card v235: the TP2 texts cannot be the reference, and the plans that serve pair profiles (warm, control,
# forced-cap, control-below) cannot run on four cards. C2_GATE_AUDITS stays at its default: the prestage and fused-commit audits
# are not ported to four cards, and the mixed plan forces them on, so mixed is not in this window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives
# the window (the graft directory and the graft binary digest of the one-card harnesses); every other value is final.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image S0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_GATE_JIT=record: the kernel cache has no four-card entries and no warm plan exists at four cards, so the first arm compiles;
# judging kernel-cache growth (the default on an S2 profile) would fail it for that. The growth is recorded, not judged.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm one engine build 10-30 min plus 5-15 min of streams; two arms 35-75 min; a
# reproduced divergence re-runs both arms once: up to 150 min. The gate budgets itself against the step limit (380 min).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,16384,32768,60000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=512
C2_GATE_JIT=record
